# Template Architecture

## Core rule

Templates are **presentation only**. They render UI from `WeddingData`; they never fetch DB, auth, payments, or business logic.

```tsx
<TemplateRenderer templateId="royal" data={weddingData} isPreview suppressMusicPlayer />
```

`TemplateProps`: `data`, optional `isPreview` (editor embedded preview), optional `suppressMusicPlayer` (publish dialog).

## Scalability (many templates)

- Register each template **once** in `src/templates/registry.ts`.
- This registry is metadata only and must not import template components. Add the SSR-enabled dynamic loader in `runtime-registry.tsx`; its keys are checked against TemplateId derived from metadata. Only TemplateRenderer imports runtime loaders. Legacy IDs resolve through `template-ids.ts`.
- Preserve template CSS in the existing runtime modules. Use the shared ModalSurface inline for template lightboxes/openers so their theme variables and zoom remain inherited; avoid independent body locks/global Escape listeners.
- Same `WeddingData` for editor, preview, DB `content` JSONB, and `/w/[slug]`.
- Bespoke `sections/` per template is expected; shared **contracts** + **preview ids** keep the editor stable.
- Do not duplicate marketing cards in `src/data/templates.ts`.

## Folder structure

```
src/templates/
  TemplateRenderer.tsx
  registry.ts
  runtime-registry.tsx
  template-ids.ts
  shared/ { components, motion, sections, theme }
  /<template-id>/
    <Name>Template.tsx
    theme.ts
    components/   # optional cinematic kit
    hooks/          # optional
    sections/
```

Example: `src/templates/royal/RoyalTemplate.tsx`.

## Shared data

All templates consume **`WeddingData`** from `src/types/`.

## Reusability (pragmatic)

- **Shared:** motion presets, theme provider, section contracts, preview ids, `isValidDisplayUrl`, optional atoms in `shared/components/`
- **Bespoke per template:** section layouts and template-specific `components/` (cinematic intro, scratch reveal, etc.)
- Do not force identical section UI across templates

## Section flow (storytelling)

Optional intro → Hero → Couple → Countdown → Blessing → Events → Story → Gallery → RSVP → Venue → Thank You.

## Events

Indian events (Mehendi, Haldi, Wedding, Reception, Sangeet): title, icon, description, date, time, venue, `googleMapLink`.

## Theme

`TemplateThemeProvider` + per-template `theme.ts` defaults. `WeddingData.theme` overrides. Pass `typographyScale` from `data.typography` for editor zoom.

Use `var(--template-primary)`, `var(--template-text)`, etc. The provider's `.template-theme` boundary isolates these colors and legacy semantic variables from studio light/dark overrides. Photo-overlay text uses separate `--template-on-image`/muted tokens. Keep overlays inline and compensate 44px action hit areas for typography zoom.

Demo previews receive server-created `createDemoWeddingData(referenceIso)` using the shared demo-date calculator; the static sample is a date-free scaffold. Do not recompute the demo calendar inside client render or advance saved user dates. Use explicit timezone date labels. Motion, keyboard and theme contract/deferred cases: `docs/mobile-motion-theme-and-demos.md`.

## Section contracts

`src/templates/shared/sections/types.ts` — same props shape; bespoke JSX inside each template.

## Preview section IDs

`src/templates/shared/sections/preview-ids.ts` — required on mapped sections:

| Section | Id |
|---------|-----|
| Hero | `PREVIEW_SECTION_IDS.hero` |
| Couple | `PREVIEW_SECTION_IDS.couple` |
| Countdown | `PREVIEW_SECTION_IDS.countdown` |
| Events | `PREVIEW_SECTION_IDS.events` |
| Story | `PREVIEW_SECTION_IDS.story` |
| Gallery | `PREVIEW_SECTION_IDS.gallery` |
| Venue | `PREVIEW_SECTION_IDS.venue` |
| RSVP | `PREVIEW_SECTION_IDS.rsvp` |

Blessing / Thank You: not in editor scroll map unless product adds panels.

## Registry

`/preview/<template-id>` works when registry `id` matches.

## Animations

Framer Motion; `src/templates/shared/motion/presets.ts`. Royal cinematic kit lives in `royal/components/` — optional for other templates. See `animations.mdc`.

## Performance

- `next/image` + `sizes`
- `isValidDisplayUrl()` before user images
- Countdown: client `mounted` guard (no SSR/client number mismatch)
- Lazy or lightweight gallery/maps; no unoptimized video heroes
- Consider `next/dynamic` for heavy below-fold sections when bundle grows

